Z||000000||CW85T-Type||03-24-2000||04:29 PM||||Car is a 1985 2m6 SE.<P>1.  Heater core.  Is it an easy job to do on these cars?  I did one in a 85 mustang I had and it was a bear (8hrs)<P>2.  My idle seems to hunt a bit.  will go between 600 and 1000 rpm.  What causes this and how do I fix it?<P>3.  Where is the optional subwoofer put on these cars, mine doesn't have one, but I want to add it.<P>Thanks A Bunch!<P>Chris Wilson||||reg||5
Z||000001||sluppy123||03-24-2000||05:23 PM||||1. The heater core is easy to replace. open the front hood and unhook the hoses giong in and out of the core, passenger side, then look up into the passenger footwell and take out the two bolts you can see in the heater core housing, I always take out the LF speaker to get the third bolt out, it's on the top towards the front of the car. pull the old one out, put the new one in.<P>2. Idle sounds about right, most fiero v-6's have a uneven idle<P>3.the factory sub is located up inside the passenger side footwell, right by the heater core case, if you have a sub you need to remove it to replace the heater core.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
